{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent legal battles that followed. the film is directed by david fincher, and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and fast paced dialogue. the movie stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is struggling to find his place in the world. he is a brilliant computer programmer, but he is also socially awkward and has a hard time connecting with people. after a painful breakup with his girlfriend, erica albright, zuckerberg creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the website becomes a huge success, but it also gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university administration.\n\nas the movie progresses, we see zuckerberg team up with his friends eduardo saverin and the winklevoss twins, cameron and tyler, to create a new website called thefacebook. the website is designed to be a social networking site exclusively for harvard students, but it quickly gains popularity and spreads to other colleges and universities.\n\nhowever, as the website grows in popularity, zuckerberg and his friends begin to have disagreements about the direction of the company. eduardo saverin wants to monetize the site through advertising, while zuckerberg wants to keep it free and open to all users. the winklevoss twins, who claim to have come up with the idea for the site, begin to sue zuckerberg for stealing their idea.\n\nthe movie explores the themes of friendship, loyalty, and the consequences of success. it also raises questions about the nature of identity and community in the digital age. the film features a talented cast, including justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, and rooney mara as erica albright, zuckerberg's girlfriend.\n\noverall, the social network is a well made and engaging movie that explores the complexities of the digital age. the film features strong performances from the cast, and the dialogue is witty and engaging. the movie also raises important questions about the consequences of success and the nature of identity and community in the digital age. it is a must see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the impact of social media on our lives.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.06196817383170128}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0031907858792692423}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -1.3194609880447388}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0003718638326972723}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.31486496329307556}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.20519337058067322}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.01832624524831772}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -6.007967749610543e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.4740769863128662}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.28426361083984375}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0007120219524949789}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.1537068784236908}, {"token": " legal", "logprob": -0.80816650390625}, {"token": " battles", "logprob": -0.0009205871028825641}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00012158608296886086}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -1.568666934967041}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -8.308542601298541e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00020382710499688983}, {"token": 